  "result": "Perfect! All 77 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Created src/render.js:**\n- `renderInvoiceText(invoice)` \u2014 renders a plain-text invoice with:\n  - First line: invoice number (or \"DRAFT\" if not issued)\n  - Second line: customer name (from database, or customer ID as fallback)\n  - One line per invoice line showing: `<qty> <name> <unitPrice> <lineTotal>`\n  - Final line: `Total: <formatted total>`\n  - All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()` from src/money.js\n\n**Example output:**\n```\nDRAFT\nNorthwind Studio\n5 Design work (hour) \u20ac85.00 \u20ac425.00\n3 Development (hour) \u20ac95.00 \u20ac285.00\nTotal: \u20ac710.00\n```\n\n**Created test/render.test.js with 14 tests covering:**\n- Draft vs issued invoice display\n- Customer name lookup and fallback\n- Currency formatting (euros, thousands separator, two decimals)\n- Line quantities, names, unit prices, and totals\n- Multiple lines and single lines\n- Large quantities and amounts\n- Different VAT rates\n- Output structure and format\n- Zero price handling\n- Multiline output verification\n\nAll amounts throughout are formatted using `formatEuros()` for consistent presentation to customers.",
